{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009175-harry-potter-and-the-ascension-war","id":1009175,"title":"Harry Potter and the Ascension War","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-27T21:52:18-08:00","id":1009175,"title":"Harry Potter and the Ascension War","content":"Im sorry, im so bloody sorry.<br /> <br /> i havent read all the books, but all of my players are Huge Harry Potter fans, they spend hours arguing &quot;how much arete dumbledoor or voldemort has&quot; &quot; is voldemort a Nephandi?&quot; &quot;what about Grindelwald.&quot; and so on<br /> <br /> so... i thought it would be interesting to see how the forums could adapt Harry Potter character's and lore in the Mage the Ascension Setting.<br /> Are you ready for the task?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T22:10:36-08:00","id":1009179,"title":"","content":"Neither would be Nephandi, as neither deal with demons. They'd both be fanatical splinter-factions of the Hermetics. A splinter-faction that regards Mages as superior beings. Basically they'd be throwbacks to the worst days of the Dark Ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T00:01:23-08:00","id":1009213,"title":"","content":"The Harry Potter books don't really paint &quot;Dark Wizards&quot; as being categorically evil to the point of being devoted to Anti-Life, so they may or may not be comparable to Nephandi. &quot;Dark Wizard&quot; in this context could just indicate they are bastards, having compromised their moral fiber in search of power and glory. It's been a while since I read the books, so I can't say much about Grindelwald (point of fact, I had to Google search because I completely forgot who that was).<br /> <br /> Voldemort, though, is pretty simple, as characters go. He's a wizard full of hubris and pride, while at the same time being crippled by dread of his own mortality. He fears death more than anything, and is willing to abandon all scruples in the quest to cheat death (and take over the world, <a href=\"https://youtu.be/1W7c8QghPxk\" target=\"_blank\">of course</a>). If this were Mage, he'd be the textbook example of the type of Hermetic who would seek out the rote for Lichdom and dive right in without hesitation or a moment of regret.<br /> <br /> From his power levels, he might be a Master, albeit possibly a specialized one. He might have Mind 5, depending on whether you think he had the ability to disconnect his psyche from his body. I'm unsure of how one would translate the creation of Horcruxes to Mage. I know for a fact he has Entropy 4, since his favorite tactic is to spam instant death against his enemies. He might also have Time 4, which he combines with Entropy 3 and Correspondence 3(?) to make it so every time someone in the world says his name, he's informed of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T00:10:32-08:00","id":1009216,"title":"","content":"Why Time 4 for the name-calling effect?<br /> It is not hanging but continuous.<br /> As long as the effect runs, you are informed of instances of speaking your name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T00:25:26-08:00","id":1009222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009175-harry-potter-and-the-ascension-war?p=1009216#post1009216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why Time 4 for the name-calling effect?<br /> It is not hanging but continuous.<br /> As long as the effect runs, you are informed of instances of speaking your name.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hanging because it's not running all the time. It only procs when someone says his name. Time 4 makes an Effect capable of going off, not just the one time, but many times. The Mage books sometimes talk about Effects that were tied to bloodlines, going off every generation or so. So long as he rolls a butt ton of successes, he could keep the Effect reoccurring for years. Which is probably the point.<br /> <br /> That said, you are correct. He could just have an Effect running continuously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T00:44:16-08:00","id":1009226,"title":"","content":"You are right.<br /> <br /> I totally forgot about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T05:39:47-08:00","id":1009287,"title":"","content":"Considering that Harry Potter lives in a world where Centaurs, Trolls, Elves, Goblins, Unicorns, and the like are all real and fairly commonplace, it's possible that these Offshoot Hermetics Wizarding World is actually a part of the Near Dreaming where Fairies hang about, a part which is kept alive by a select few Hermetics who spend a great deal of time defending it and reinforcing the Reality Zones that keep Galmour in high supply. Perhaps this offshoot have been doing this for so long and so successfully that generations after, they are no longer in connection with the majority of their Tradition, perhaps to the point of most not being aware of other traditions at all.<br /> <br /> If this world was the case, then the Statute of Secrecy is an even bigger deal than it would be otherwise because any intrusion by Banal people would be paramount to death of this world, Thus telling anyone about the Wizarding World could cause the world to become permanently cut off from mundane reality, and all its inhabitants to suffer Chimeric Death or worse.<br /> <br /> This would also explain why Wizards tend to ignore or push aside modern technology in its entirety. They carry too much banality and thus would harm the denizens of the land they inhabit. In a strange way, this may mean Voldermort had partially noble intentions as getting rid of all sleepers and anyone attached to them would mean reducing the risk of Banality entering the world and killing it. However, his actions would make him much more like the Technocracy in terms of approach. Providing and enforcing absolute control all in the name of safety and power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T19:59:58-08:00","id":1009608,"title":"","content":"I hope your players expand their perspective a bit. Viewing everything through the lens of something you're more comfortable with is a limiting way to live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T20:28:12-08:00","id":1009619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009175-harry-potter-and-the-ascension-war?p=1009608#post1009608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope your players expand their perspective a bit. Viewing everything through the lens of something you're more comfortable with is a limiting way to live.</div> </div> </div> </div>its just off game talk xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T21:13:25-08:00","id":1009628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009175-harry-potter-and-the-ascension-war?p=1009608#post1009608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope your players expand their perspective a bit. Viewing everything through the lens of something you're more comfortable with is a limiting way to live.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coincidentally, this is a major theme of Mage: The Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T08:18:44-08:00","id":1009796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009175-harry-potter-and-the-ascension-war?p=1009213#post1009213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Voldemort, though, is pretty simple, as characters go. He's a wizard full of hubris and pride, while at the same time being crippled by dread of his own mortality. He fears death more than anything, and is willing to abandon all scruples in the quest to cheat death (and take over the world, <a href=\"https://youtu.be/1W7c8QghPxk\" target=\"_blank\">of course</a>). If this were Mage, he'd be the textbook example of the type of Hermetic who would seek out the rote for Lichdom and dive right in without hesitation or a moment of regret.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding to this : His fear of mortality and his gruesome methods point at a rather deep bout with Jhor. He is essentially mini Voormas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T12:56:25-08:00","id":1009904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009175-harry-potter-and-the-ascension-war?p=1009796#post1009796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Adding to this : His fear of mortality and his gruesome methods point at a rather deep bout with Jhor. He is essentially mini Voormas.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, and leads me to my next point. Voldemort probably has either Jhor Resonance (or Synergy, if we're going with M20) or a Jhor (Morbid) Quiet. Maybe both. He certainly looks like he's been warped by the death taint, if we're judging by his film appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T13:13:52-08:00","id":1009913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009175-harry-potter-and-the-ascension-war?p=1009904#post1009904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is true, and leads me to my next point. Voldemort probably has either Jhor Resonance (or Synergy, if we're going with M20) or a Jhor (Morbid) Quiet. Maybe both. He certainly looks like he's been warped by the death taint, if we're judging by his film appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't you think it could be some harsh paradox blacklash due to his way to vulgar experiences to become immortal ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T18:59:12-08:00","id":1010027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009175-harry-potter-and-the-ascension-war?p=1009913#post1009913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Don't you think it could be some harsh paradox blacklash due to his way to vulgar experiences to become immortal ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well...that would explain why he has no nose...or how his narcissism became his own personal downfall","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}